For fixed \(\rho\in I\), define the first augmented randomized action by
\[
\mathcal A_{n,1}^{\mathrm{aug}}
=\bigl((H_{n,s}(\rho),Z_{n1s})\bigr)_{s\in S}.
\]
On \(\prod_{s\in S}\Omega_{n,1s}(\rho)\), its known design mass is
\[
q_{n,1}^{\mathrm{aug}}(a)
=\prod_{s\in S}
\left\{
\binom{N_{n1s}}{\lfloor\rho N_{n1s}\rfloor}
\binom{N_{n1s}}{m_{n1s}}
\right\}^{-1}.
\]
The first-stage selector is the measurable map sending the augmented action and observed responses to the complete label \(C_n(\rho)\).  Given the first-stage history and label \(C\), define the second action by \(\mathcal A_{n,2}= (Z_{n2s})_{s:C_s=1}\), with conditional mass \(\prod_{s:C_s=1}\binom{N_{n2s}}{m_{n2s}}^{-1}\); it has no coordinate for \(C_s=0\).  This is the augmented-action representation of the two-stage design.
